From be188278a82d2a018627c0fbe7dc57bc711941f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xolani <xolani@example.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 08:20:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix RC1-H-002: unique-learner error counting + targetGroups
 field mismatch

- services/errorAnalysisService.js: performErrorAnalysis() now tracks a
  Set of unique affected learner names per topic (parsing question_data
  per learner the same way itemAnalysisService.js does, same half-marks
  threshold) instead of summing per-question failure counts across all
  questions sharing a topic. frequency is now that Set's size, so
  '% of learners affected' can never exceed 100%.
- services/interventionPlanService.js: generateInterventionPlan() now
  returns targetGroups (array) alongside the existing targetGroup
  (display string), so interventionReportsService.js's existing read
  of targetGroups resolves instead of silently defaulting to [].
- docs/releases/RC1-MILESTONE.md: recorded root-cause analysis and fix
  under RC1-H-002 in the Defect Log, updated the Phase A Assessment
  'Item analysis / blueprint analytics' row.
- Verified via standalone reproduction of the exact seeded scenario
  (5 learners, 2 questions/topic): old formula reproduces 140%/0
  exactly as observed in production; fixed formula produces 80%/4.
  npm test could not be run in this sandbox (npm install blocked on
  an unrelated sheetjs CDN dependency) -- recommend running the real
  test suite and a fresh WhatsApp NEW TEST/capture pass against the
  existing seeded blueprint (ID 1) before marking RC1-H-002 Resolved.
